From 10716f7aefc6b7979d958e5522d44a75d36f5078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:39:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: fail closed on unresolvable stdin
 into nested login shells

A login/interactive shell the command starts (su -l, sudo -i, doas -s, ssh host, bash -l, ...)
holds aliases of its own, so its stdin is walked with unknown alias names. Four stdin shapes
were skipped instead (t_f7fd81411e70a5a2, from review t_d2f6f4ea26c9f1a9 of #3039; all
pre-existing, equally open at #2911's head):

1. fd duplication onto stdin: `su -l bob 0<&3 3< f`, `{ su -l bob; } <&3 3< f`,
   `exec 3< f; { su -l bob; } 0<&3`, `su -l bob < /dev/fd/3 3< f`. Now the descriptor's
   input redirections anywhere in the command (`N< f`, `N<> f`, `N<<< T`) are its sources.
2. process substitution: `su -l bob < <(cat f)`, `while ...; do su -l bob; done < <(cat f)`.
3. unresolvable targets: `su -l bob < $S`, `< "$S"`, `< $(echo f)`, `` < `echo f` ``, `< *.sh`.
4. a redirection on a call to a function the command defines: `f() { su -l bob; }; f < f`,
   `f <<< T`, `f <<EOF`, also through another function (`g() { f; }; g < f`).

(1) and (4) are walked as the shell's script. A source the walk cannot name (2, 3, a
descriptor with no source or a heredoc source behind `0<&N`) is now refused with a named
reason ("the guard cannot resolve `$S`, the stdin of a login/interactive shell it starts")
in executed text; a mere mention is not.

Controls stay allowed under {zz}: `cat 0<&3 3< f`, `su -l bob < /dev/null`, `su -l bob 0<&-`,
`{ cat; } < <(cat f)`, `cat < $S`, `f() { cat; }; f < f`, `f() { su -l bob; }; cat < f`.

Tests: RED->GREEN in tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_session_aliases.py
(_NESTED_FOREIGN_SHELLS +17, new test_nested_login_shell_unresolvable_stdin_fails_closed x15,
controls +13, mention-not-refused +1; executed-guard mutant killed).
---
